{\*\ftnsep\chftnsep}\pgndec\pard\plain \s1\keep\sb360\sa80\keepn\cf18\rtlch\af8\afs40\ltrch\hich\af5\afs40\dbch\af8\loch\f5\fs40\keep\sb360\sa80\keepn{
{\*\bkmkstart _fdbc99e31f93917b7f2a3dbe014f2b1a612a410}Record count}
\par \pard\plain \s97{
FlexCel Reports need to know in advance how much records to insert. But some DataSet components in Delphi don't return the correct RecordCount, and we need to supply the number of rows to it. For more information read the section }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://doc.tmssoftware.com/flexcel/vcl/guides/reports-developer-guide.html#about-record-count-in-datasets" }{\fldrslt {\cf20
About Record Count in DataSets}{}}}
 in the Report developer\u8217\'92s guide.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\keep\sb160\sa80\keepn\cf18\rtlch\af8\afs32\ltrch\hich\af5\afs32\dbch\af8\loch\f5\fs32{
{\*\bkmkstart _concepts}Concepts}
\par \pard\plain \s97{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af10\ltrch \u-3913\'3f\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-360\li720\lin720{
We will be using ADO with a }{\rtlch\ab\ltrch\b
CursorType}{
 set to }{\rtlch\ab\ltrch\b
ctOpenForwardOnly}{
. In this mode the record count returned is -1 (the other demos in this section use the default CursorType)}
\par \pard\plain \s97{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af10\ltrch \u-3913\'3f\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-360\li720\lin720{
We are showing 2 different ways to count the records:}
\par \pard\plain \s97{\listtext\pard\plain  1.\tab}\ilvl1\ls2 \fi-360\li1440\lin1440{
By using a __FLEXCELCOUNT field.}
\par \pard\plain \s97{\listtext\pard\plain  2.\tab}\ilvl1\ls2 \fi-360\li1440\lin1440{
By setting the parameter }{\rtlch\ab\ltrch\b
recordCountMode}{
 to SlowCount when calling }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://doc.tmssoftware.com/flexcel/vcl/api/FlexCel.Report/TFlexCelReport/AddTable.html" }{\fldrslt {\cf20
TFlexCelReport.AddTable}{}}}
 or }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://doc.tmssoftware.com/flexcel/vcl/api/FlexCel.Report/TFlexCelReport/AddConnection.html" }{\fldrslt {\cf20
TFlexCelReport.AddConnection}{}}}
.}
\par \pard\plain \s106\fi0\li480\lin480\ri480\rin480\sb100\sa100{
[!Note]}
\par \pard\plain \s106\fi0\li480\lin480\ri480\rin480\sb100\sa100\fi0\li480\lin480\ri480\rin480\sb100\sa100{
{\*\bkmkstart _fdbc99e31f93917b7f2a3dbe014f2b1a612a410}{\*\bkmkstart _concepts}In this specific case setting SlowCount to true isn't strictly necessary. As RecordCount is -1, FlexCel can figure out that the number is wrong and do the slow count automatically. You need to specify SlowCount for those components that return the number of records fetched, like for example 25 because in those cases FlexCel can't know that this number isn't the real record count.{\*\bkmkend _fdbc99e31f93917b7f2a3dbe014f2b1a612a410}{\*\bkmkend _concepts}}
\par }